There are C(7,2) = 21 favorable outcomes out of 2^7 = 128. Thus the probability is 21/128 = \frac{21}{128}.

**最终答案**

\frac{21}{128}

Productive time is 150/60 = \frac{5}{2} hours. Therefore the number printed is 21 times \frac{5}{2} = \frac{105}{2}.

**最终答案**

\frac{105}{2}

There are 4 ordered pairs with this sum among 36 equally likely outcomes, so the probability is 4/36 = \frac{1}{9}.

**最终答案**

\frac{1}{9}

Use the complement: P(no success) = (1/2)^6 = \frac{1}{64}. Therefore P(at least one) = 1 - that value = \frac{63}{64}.

**最终答案**

\frac{63}{64}

Favorable selections are C(5,1)C(8,2) = 140; all selections are C(13,3) = 286. The probability is 140/286 = \frac{70}{143}.

**最终答案**

\frac{70}{143}
